.TH BACPACK 1 "2026-08-14" "bacpack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bacpack \- read and write ManageBac from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacpack
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a student's own ManageBac pages over an ordinary session cookie,
downloads a class's files, and writes the two
plain text forms ManageBac exposes: CAS experiences and Learner Portfolio
entries.
The official ManageBac+ API is administrator-only, so this drives the web
interface instead.
.PP
Reads are live and nothing is cached, except for the session cookie
(see
.BR FILES )
and files you ask
.B \-\-download
to save. Every write prints a preview and exits without sending;
.B \-\-confirm
is what actually posts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANAGEBAC_SCHOOL
Required. The subdomain of your school's ManageBac, e.g.
.B acme
for acme.managebac.com.
.TP
.BR MANAGEBAC_EMAIL ", " MANAGEBAC_PASSWORD
Your ManageBac login. Checked before the credentials file, so CI can pass them
without writing anything to disk.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/managebac/credentials
Your ManageBac email on line 1, your password on line 2. Mode 600. The
environment variables
.B MANAGEBAC_EMAIL
and
.B MANAGEBAC_PASSWORD
take precedence.
.TP
.I ~/.config/managebac/cookie
The cached
.B _managebac_session
value, written by bacpack itself. Sessions last about a fortnight, not the year
the cookie advertises; when one dies bacpack logs in again and rewrites this
file. A cookie pasted here by hand is used as-is, which avoids storing a
password.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B due
Upcoming deadlines. ManageBac prints dates without a year, so it is inferred:
a month and day
already past belongs to next year. Teachers post duplicate deadlines, so only
exact
title-plus-time collisions are removed.
.TP
.B classes
Your classes and their ids.
.TP
.B cas list
CAS experiences with hours, badges and reflection counts.
.TP
.B cas outcomes
The seven IB learning outcomes and their ids, read live because they are per
school.
.TP
.B cas groups
School groups an experience can be attached to.
.TP
.B "cas add"
Create a CAS experience.
.TP
.B "cas edit \-\-experience \fINAME\fR"
Change one. Anything not passed keeps its current value.
.TP
.B "cas delete \-\-experience \fINAME\fR"
Remove one, after showing its hours and reflection count.
.TP
.B "cas reflect \-\-experience \fINAME\fB \-\-body\-file \fIFILE\fR"
Add a reflection. Body only: the form carries no other usable field.
.TP
.B "task \fITITLE\fB [\-\-class \fINAME\fB] [\-\-download \fIDIR\fB]"
One upcoming task: the description the teacher wrote and the files attached to
it. \fITITLE\fR is part of the task title, or its \fI/student/...\fR url from
\fBdue \-\-json\fR. When two classes set the same title, the command lists
both and asks for \fB\-\-class\fR. \fB\-\-download\fR saves the attachments
under \fIDIR/<task title>/\fR. Only tasks still listed by \fBdue\fR can be found.
.TP
.B "class units|files|discussions \-\-class \fINAME\fR"
Unit plans, every file in the class, or discussion posts. A discussion carries
its date, category, author and body, and the body keeps its line breaks because
that is how teachers list exercises. Only the first page is read, which is five
posts: the rest sits behind a \fIShow More\fR button whose route is not mapped.
.TP
.B "class files \-\-class \fINAME\fB [\-\-match \fITEXT\fB] \-\-download \fIDIR\fR"
Save the files under \fIDIR/<class name>/<folder>/\fR, keeping the folder
layout, or all of them if \fB\-\-match\fR is omitted. Files already on disk are
skipped, so an interrupted run resumes by running it again. One ManageBac
folder can hold two different files under the same name, so later ones are
numbered \fIname\-2.pdf\fR rather than overwriting. No \fB\-\-confirm\fR: this
writes to your disk, not to ManageBac.
.TP
.B "portfolio list \-\-class \fINAME\fR"
Learner Portfolio entries with their tags. The index is paginated at ten
entries a page and every page is read, so this is the whole portfolio and not
the newest ten.
.TP
.B "portfolio tags \-\-class \fINAME\fR"
The works and the full tag taxonomy, grouped by category. Works change every
September.
.TP
.B "portfolio add \-\-class \fINAME\fB \-\-body\-file \fIFILE\fR"
Add an entry. There is no title field; fold the title into the body HTML.
.TP
.B "portfolio edit \-\-class \fINAME\fB \-\-id \fIN\fR"
Change an entry. Anything not passed keeps its current value.
.TP
.B "portfolio star|delete \-\-class \fINAME\fB \-\-id \fIN\fR"
Toggle the star, or remove the entry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm
Actually send the write. Without it, every write previews and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output. Available on every read. \fBtask \-\-download\fR ignores it.
.TP
.BI \-\-class " NAME"
Part of a class name, not an id: \fB\-\-class greek\fR. Ids change each school
year, and every
class exposes the portfolio route, so a name is both safer and shorter.
On \fBtask\fR it narrows a title that two classes share instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Limit \fBdue\fR to the next N days.
.TP
.BI \-\-match " TEXT"
On \fBclass files\fR, keep only the files whose \fIfolder/name\fR contains
\fITEXT\fR, case-insensitively. One flag for both a folder and a filename:
\fB\-\-match "paper 2"\fR or \fB\-\-match annotated\fR. Matching nothing is an
error, not an empty result.
.TP
.BI \-\-download " DIR"
On \fBclass files\fR, save every file under \fIDIR\fR instead of listing them.
On \fBtask\fR, save the task's attachments under \fIDIR/<task title>/\fR.
Takes no \fB\-\-confirm\fR: it writes to your disk, not to ManageBac.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " TEXT" ", " \-\-start " ISO" ", " \-\-end " ISO"
On \fBcas add\fR and \fBcas edit\fR: the experience name and its dates.
.TP
.BI \-\-experience " NAME"
Part of an experience name. Used by \fBcas edit\fR, \fBdelete\fR and \fBreflect\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-id " N"
The entry id, as shown by \fBportfolio list \-\-json\fR. Used by \fBportfolio edit\fR, \fBstar\fR and \fBdelete\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-group " NAME"
Part of a school group name, as listed by \fBcas groups\fR. Settable only when the experience is created.
.TP
.BI \-\-notes\-file " FILE"
CAS experience notes, read from \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-project
Mark the experience as a CAS project. Off unless passed.
.TP
.BI \-\-supervisor\-name " TEXT" ", " \-\-supervisor\-title " TEXT" ", " \-\-supervisor\-email " TEXT" ", " \-\-supervisor\-phone " TEXT"
The CAS supervisor's details.
.TP
.BI \-\-creativity " H" ", " \-\-action " H" ", " \-\-service " H"
Hours per CAS strand.
.TP
.BI \-\-service\-type " TYPE"
One of direct, indirect, advocacy, research.
.TP
.BI \-\-approaches " LIST"
Comma separated: ongoing, school-based, community-based, individual.
.TP
.BI \-\-outcomes " LIST"
Comma separated learning outcome names.
.TP
.BI \-\-tags " LIST" ", " \-\-works " LIST"
Comma separated portfolio taxonomy values. Punctuation is flattened before
matching, so values
copied from another system resolve even when their commas differ. Qualify an
ambiguous label as
\fBConcepts/Culture\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-notify\-advisor
Email the CAS advisor when the experience is created. Off unless passed.
.B cas add
only: the ManageBac edit form has no such field, so
.B cas edit
rejects it. The checkbox ships pre-ticked, so bacpack always sends the
field explicitly.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
stdout carries exactly one JSON value and nothing else; errors stay on stderr
with a non-zero exit status, so consumers branch on the exit code rather than
parsing the error. A read that legitimately finds nothing is an empty array,
not an error.
.TP
.B due
An array of
.IR "{title, subject, when, due, badges, action, url}" .
Teacher duplicates are kept rather than merged, so the same task can appear
twice under different subjects.
.TP
.B classes
An array of
.IR "{id, name}" .
Ids change each school year; match on
.I name
instead.
.TP
.B cas list
An array of
.IR "{id, name, badges, hours, reflections}" .
.TP
.B task
One object,
.IR "{title, subject, when, due, badges, action, url, description, attachments}" .
.I attachments
is an array of
.IR "{name, size, path}" .
With
.B \-\-download
it prints a one-line summary instead and ignores
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B cas outcomes
An array of
.IR "{id, label}" .
.TP
.B cas groups
An array of
.IR "{id, label}" .
.TP
.B class units
An array of
.IR "{id, title, status, badges}" .
.TP
.B class files
An array of
.IR "{name, folder, size, url}" .
The
.I url
is a pre-signed CDN link fetched fresh for this response and it expires, so
download from it now rather than storing it.
.TP
.B class discussions
An array of
.IR "{id, title, author, category, postedAt, posted, body, url}" .
.I category
and
.I postedAt
are null when ManageBac prints no category or an unparseable date;
.I posted
always carries the date exactly as printed.
.TP
.B portfolio list
An array of
.IR "{id, date, tags, body}" .
.I body
is plain text, not the original HTML: it is for skimming, not for editing and
sending back.
.TP
.B portfolio tags
One object,
.I works
and
.IR tags ,
each an array of the values that class accepts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non-zero on a rejected login, an unresolvable class or tag, or a page that parsed
to nothing.
The last case means ManageBac changed its markup, not that there is no work due.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bun (1)
